;; world/rooms/glasswood/x-2y6.room
(room
  region: glasswood
  at: (-2 6)
  title: "The Ice Well"
  intent: "a well of clear ice going down from the meltwater to a cold blue stone: somewhere deeper, not yet"
  bed: (wind 0.0 water 0.9 hum 0.4 drone 0.6)
  light: 0.25
  grid:
  ("########~~~##############"
   "########~~~##############"
   "########~~~##############"
   "####    ~~~##############"
   "####    ~~~##############"
   "########~~~##############"
   "########~~~##############"
   "########~~~##############"
   "########~~~##############"
   "########~~~o#############"
   "#########################")
  things: ((ring-stone at: (11 9) overtone: 4)
           (lantern-moth at: (6 3) count: 3 drawn: 3))
  decor: auto)
;; Down from the Meltwater's pool. Halfway, air is trapped under the ice
;; in a pocket to the west (rows 3-4): a place to rest and look down. At
;; the bottom a cold blue stone (H4) is set in the east wall: it hums D4,
;; shivers off-key at what you carry, and stays shut. Nothing in this
;; release gives H4. Proposed (question 5's reply on the map): the door
;; to Wrongwater.
